+## Q4 — The missing fixture
+
+The fixture is synthetic and source-shaped. It has three eligible rows, all with energy 1 and zero residual:
+
+| row | kind | demand-capped bits | resulting live term |
+| ---: | --- | ---: | --- |
+| 0 | incumbent | 10 | none |
+| 1 | association change | 11 | C1 = +1 |
+| 2 | adjacent-mode offset | 12 | C2 = +2 |
+
+At exact `eta=1`, FACTORIAL's own `compact_anchor` classifies and constructs the terms. `DROP_C2` scores row 1 highest and selects index 1. `FULL` adds C2, scores row 2 highest, and selects index 2.
+
+**PASS — `DROP_C2=1`, `FULL=2`.** The two arms differ, so C2 survives construction and reaches the argmax. This is the decisive wiring result.
